Input: {"question": "When was the Kansas City Southern Depot built?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d00", "start": 0, "end": 199, "text": "Kansas City Southern Depot, Zwolle The Kansas City Southern Depot is a former Kansas City Southern Railway station located at the intersection of Spanish and Port Arthur Streets in Zwolle, Louisiana."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d00", "start": 200, "end": 292, "text": "Built in 1914, the depot is the only surviving building connected to the railroad in Zwolle."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d00", "start": 293, "end": 459, "text": "The railroad was built through the Zwolle area in 1896, and the town was founded shortly thereafter; the 1914 depot was a replacement for the town's original station."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d00", "start": 460, "end": 617, "text": "The railway station was an important shipping center for the town's lumber industry; lumber was Sabine Parish's chief export from the early 1900s through the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d01", "start": 0, "end": 451, "text": "Room KCT Board Room Regnier Extreme Screen Theatre Science City Check Availability Science City Planetarium Movie Theatre Live Theatre 000 Years of Union Station 1914-2014 Union Station 1903 1906 1910 1914 1917 1921 1933 1945 1950-1970 1968 1972 1973 1974 1979-1986 1983 1988 1994 1996 1999 2002 2005 2006 2008 2010 2011 2012 2013 1903 The second great Kansas City flood consumes the railroad station (Union Depot) in the city’s West Bottoms district."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2ac984:d01", "start": 452, "end": 552, "text": "Rail executives decide to build a new train station on higher ground and in a more central location."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0411-1ad3fa2